{title: 012 - Joyful, Joyful, We Adore Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #012 • HYMN TO JOY • 15.15.15.15}
{lyricist: Henry van Dyke}
{composer: Ludwig van Beethoven}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 12}
{meta: tune HYMN TO JOY}
{meta: meter 15.15.15.15}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Joyful, joyful, [Bm]we adore [Am]Thee, [G]God [F#dim]of [G]glory, Lord [F#dim]of [G]love;
[G]Heats unfold [F#dim]like flow'rs [G/D]before [C]Thee, Hail [Bm]Thee as [C]the sun [G/D]above.
[Em/B]Melt the clouds [D7/C]of sin [G/D]and [D7/C]sadness, Drive [Em/B]the [F#dim]dark of doubt [G]away;
[D]Giver [D7]of immortal gladness, [Am]Fill us [Bm]with the [Em/B]light [Am]of [D/F#]day!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]All Thy [Bm]works with [G]joy [F#dim]surround Thee,
[G]Earth and [Bm]heav'n [Am]reflect [G]Thy [F#dim]rays,
[G]Stars and [F#dim]angels [C]sing [Bm]around [G/D]Thee,
[G]Center of unbroken praise;
[Em/B]Field and [D7/C]forest, vale [F#dim]and mountain,
[Em/B]Bloss'ming [G/D]meadow, [Em/B]flashing [G]sea,
[D]Chanting [G/D]bird and [Am]flowing [Bm]fountain
[D]Call [D7]us [G/D]to [D7/C]rejoice [Bm]in [Am]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Thou art [Bm]giving [G]and [F#dim]forgiving,
[G]Ever [Bm]blessing, [G]ever [F#dim]blest,
[G]Wellspring [F#dim]of [G/D]the [C]joy [Bm]of [C]living,
[G]Oceandepth of [Bm]happy [G/D]rest!
[Em/B]Thou the [D7/C]father, Christ [Em/B]our [F#dim]Brother [G/B]-
[Em/B]All who [G/D]live [D7/C]in [Em/B]love [F#dim]are [G]Thine:
[D]Teach [D7]us [G/D]how to [Am]love [Bm]each other,
[D]Lift [D7]us [G/D]to [D7/C]the [Am]joy [Bm]divine.
{end_of_verse}
